  "rules": [
    "Frozen child cell declarations are copied verbatim from S04 specification below, including names, commands, timeouts and byte budgets. Sequential invocation only.",
    "Capture identity before and after EACH required child and native addon run. Fail on host, binary, alias or compiler drift. Fail on OS mismatch, missing aliases, compiler/build/load failure, stderr, signal, timeout or oversized output.",
    "Use fixed process.execPath child executable with frozen arguments; no arbitrary commands/paths/env override API. Explicit compiler argument is the P02 resolved binary.",
    "Reuse parseTaskTap without edits. Reject null parse, names/order/count mismatch, any skip/cancel/todo/failure/nested report, incomplete summary, budgets exceeded, hash/byte-count mismatch.",
    "Negative test observations include nested skipped child with otherwise zero exit, direct skip, todo, malformed/truncated TAP, renamed/omitted result, timeout, nonzero exit, stderr and output oversize. Keep these fixtures separate from required positive observations.",
    "Preserve complete child raw output inside diagnostic JSON (not trimmed or summarized); outer capture therefore retains reconstructable exact child stdout/stderr bytes plus hashes. No detached file artifacts unless coordinator adds exact paths before freeze.",
    "Original native flock callback remains intact. Add a separate owned-addon witness that captures actual compiler/header/source/artifact bytes and verifies real lock contention; temporary binaries are removed after identity capture.",
    "No native browser/account outputs are created. Existing kernel flock operations plus S04 real filesystem fixtures qualify only this local milestone."
  ],
